[ceiling] The two hooks' flat undersides are the snap's retention bearings: each lies flat on the funnel frame's 3 mm web, so it keeps its square face. The current native slice in integration-review/native-slice-reviews/2026-10-03-elbow-cradle-h2c-v2/ retains two bed-rooted supports beneath those bearings. Every emitted support bead has a clear outward removal sweep after its contact and branch junctions are detached. Physical retention, bearing finish and removal effort remain unqualified for the current hooks.
